---
/**
 * /local-numbers/ — Local Numbers: MNO-backed US numbers with two-way SMS.
 *
 * Built from the "Spenza Local Numbers" HTML design the way
 * /voice-observability-solution/ was built from its own: the body is
 * hand-built, and it renders through `WpLayout` so the site's header, footer,
 * demo popup, Analytics and lead-capture runtime stay exactly as they are on
 * every other page. The design's nav bar and footer are not used.
 *
 * It is one of the two pages under "Number Services" in the Solution menu, the
 * other being Voice Observability.
 *
 * Title, description, canonical, Open Graph and the schema graph — including a
 * `Service` node the WebPage names as its subject — live in `data/wp-seo.json`,
 * which is what `WpLayout` emits.
 *
 * Every slug-keyed data file points at the Voice Observability page's entries:
 * the same purged CSS bundles (this page's own styles are scoped and ship
 * separately, so the bundles only have to cover the chrome, which is
 * identical) and the same page script, which drives the header's mobile
 * submenus and opens the demo popup from any `.get-started`. Sharing the files
 * rather than copying them means a visitor arriving from that page already has
 * them cached. Do not run `wp:optimize-css` for this page — read the comment
 * in `ai-phone-number.astro` first.
 *
 * Lead capture: the design's email box only printed "We'll be in touch" and
 * sent nothing anywhere. It is now Gravity Forms 19 — "Book A Free Demo", the
 * same form that closes /controlhub/ and the other marketing pages — so
 * `hubspot-forms.js` validates it, posts it to HubSpot's `#gform_19` form,
 * replays it to WordPress for the sales alert, and replaces it with the same
 * confirmation. The hero's "Book a Demo" opens the Get Started popup, as
 * everywhere else.
 */
import WpLayout from '../layouts/WpLayout.astro';
import '../styles/local-numbers.css';

const voipList = [
  'Numbers sourced from VoIP aggregators, not licensed MNOs',
  'Shared DID ranges flagged in carrier spam databases',
  'More likely to receive lower STIR/SHAKEN attestation',
